# Line endings — normalise to LF in the repository regardless of platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.php    text diff=php
*.md     text
*.json   text
*.yml    text
*.yaml   text
*.xml    text
*.dist   text

*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.svg    text
*.sqlite binary

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Distribution
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Packagist ships `git archive` output, filtered by export-ignore. Anything
# listed here is excluded from the tarball Composer downloads for every
# consumer of this package.
#
# Keeping development scaffolding out is not cosmetic: it is downloaded and
# stored in every application's vendor/ directory, on every deploy, forever.
#
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml` has a `package` job that asserts this list is
# actually working — it fails the build if tests/ or docs/ reach the archive,
# or if src/ ever stops reaching it.

/tests               export-ignore
/tools               export-ignore
/docs                export-ignore
/.github             export-ignore
/.gitattributes      export-ignore
/.gitignore          export-ignore
/.editorconfig       export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist    export-ignore
/phpunit.xml         export-ignore
/.phpunit.cache      export-ignore
/debug_autoload.php  export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md     export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md  export-ignore
/CHANGES.md          export-ignore

# Deliberately NOT export-ignored — these are part of the package:
#   /src           the framework itself
#   /composer.json
#   /LICENSE       required for licence compliance in vendor/
#   /README.md     shown on Packagist
#   /CHANGELOG.md  users need it to decide whether to upgrade
#   /SECURITY.md   users need to know how to report a vulnerability
